{"id": 33, "ts": 1779624867.9800513, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "**PUBLIC_MESSAGE:**\nBased on the evidence we have, Candidate\u202fB still offers the strongest overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role: he is very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well, and possesses solid technical competence (weather assessment and computer skills). However, we now have confirmation that there are **no positive examples** of his crew cooperation or professional communication\u2014only negative observations (nasty remarks toward colleagues and a pretentious tone). This raises a serious concern for cockpit teamwork and safety.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC demonstrates strong stress resilience, technical competence, quick decision quality, and excellent attention, and he shows a clear concern for others, which suggests good crew orientation, though his communication difficulties and egocentric perception remain concerns. Candidate\u202fD shows excellent problem\u2011solving, responsibility, and concentration, but we lack any data on his crew cooperation, communication, or reliability, and his moody/loner traits could affect teamwork. Candidate\u202fA has strong situational awareness and leadership but lacks evidence on reliability, stress handling, and crew interaction, and his unfriendly demeanor is a red flag.\n**Key unresolved issues:**\n1. Whether Candidate\u202fB\u2019s negative communication style is an isolated issue or indicative of a broader teamwork risk.\n2. Any reliability or stress\u2011resilience evidence for Candidates\u202fA and\u202fD.\n3. Positive crew\u2011cooperation or communication evidence for Candidates\u202fC and\u202fD to weigh against their other strengths/weaknesses.\nGiven the current gaps, I recommend we **focus the next inquiry on obtaining any reliability or stress\u2011resilience observations for Candidates\u202fA and\u202fD**, and any **positive crew\u2011cooperation or communication examples for Candidates\u202fC and\u202fD**. This will allow us to compare B\u2019s strong technical profile against the overall safety\u2011critical fit of the alternatives before finalizing a recommendation."}
