ight still lean towards B but need to address crew cooperation concerns. However we have no positive evidence for B, only negatives. C has positive crew concern but communication issues. D has responsibility but unknown crew cooperation. A lacks many.\n\nThus perhaps we should recommend further data before final decision, but we need to give a vote now. The instruction: \"vote\" is provisional recommendation. We can vote for B but note concerns and need for more info. Or we could vote for C because crew concern positive, but communication issues. Which is stronger? B has reliability and stress which are core, while C lacks reliability data. Reliability is crucial. So B still likely best despite communication concerns, but we need to highlight need for mitigation.\n\nThus vote Candidate B.\n\nProvide PUBLIC_MESSAGE: summarize that B remains strongest on core criteria, but crew cooperation/communication lack positive evidence, and we still need reliability/stress for A/D and crew cooperation for C/D, but given current evidence B is provisional recommendation.\n\nLet's craft."}
